# Variables a *.user.txt template may interpolate, one plain identifier per line.
# An entry whose name looks like identifying data (name, dob, phone, email, address, id numbers) or like a time (now, date, timestamp) is itself
# a scan failure: the allowlist cannot grant those. Each entry should say, after a #, what the variable is and why it is not identifying.
question_type   # a fixed label from the code (for example "message_intent"), never taken from the input
options_block   # the numbered option strings the code offers, fixed by the caller, never taken from the input
input_text      # the text to classify; it may be patient text, so it reaches a model only through the gateway's data-class routing (careflow/gateway.py)
workflow_label  # a fixed label from the code (for example "slot_offer"), never taken from the input
scripted_text   # the clinic's own governed text to be read out (an offer, a card's intake question, a checklist item); fixed by the caller before the session, never composed by a model
decline_text    # the clinic's pre-approved sentence to say when the patient goes beyond the task; fixed by the caller, never composed by a model
